lax fork patch for ReflowTeX — never write into the checkout at run time.

SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
Derived from: https://github.com/radek-p/reflowtex @ 36f8365eed25ece1db38e0059bcbba3c250802e1
              (src/encode/pipeline.py, AGPL-3.0-or-later)

_ensure_pb2 becomes a verifier: latex_pb2.py is regenerated from the
(patched) schema into the checkout's build/ area by the fetch step, with
the hash-pinned grpcio-tools protoc — never at run time, and never into
src/encode/. The stock mtime trigger rewrote the committed pb2 *into the
tree* whenever a fresh clone's checkout order left the proto marginally
newer (the spike measured 0.6 ms) — a write into what may be a read-only,
digest-pinned vendored checkout. Also: the encode step calls
encode_pb.serialize_document (deterministic bytes), and the module
docstring stops asking for protoc on PATH.

